\section{Method}
\label{sec:method}
\label{sec:pipeline}
\label{sec:condorcet}
\label{sec:effective-k}

Self-Consistency (SC) \citep{wang2023sc} samples $K$ reasoning traces and selects the majority answer. Under correlated traces (Fleiss' $\kappa$ \citep{fleiss1971kappa}), the effective ensemble size $K_\text{eff}$ is
\begin{equation}
\label{eq:effk}
K_{\text{eff}} = K \,/\, [1 + (K{-}1) \cdot \kappa]
\end{equation}
(following \citet{ladha1992correlated}). Intuitively, $K_\text{eff}$ measures how many effectively independent votes $K$ correlated traces contribute; e.g., $K{=}12$ traces with $\kappa{=}0.69$ yield $K_\text{eff} \approx 1.4$, meaning twelve correlated traces carry no more independent information than 1.4 uncorrelated ones. This motivates constraint-based aggregation.

Symbolic Invariant Consensus Aggregation (SICA) extends SC by extracting formal constraints from traces and selecting the answer best supported by the satisfiable subset (Figure~\ref{fig:pipeline}).

\begin{table*}[t]
\centering
\small
\caption{SICA vs.\ SC across all non-degenerate self-extraction conditions (sorted by SC). Two conditions show significant degradation after Benjamini--Hochberg (BH) correction ($m{=}6$ confirmatory; remaining exploratory); no condition shows a significant gain. $\Delta$ = SICA $-$ SC (pp). PW: ProofWriter. Symbols: $^b$gold ICL; \textbf{bold}: $p < 0.05$; {*}\,BH adj.\ $p = 0.042$; $^{3s}$\,3-seed aggregate; $^{4s}$\,4-seed confirmatory aggregate; $^\dagger$\,4-seed replication in Table~\ref{tab:multi-seed} (unmarked: single-seed exploratory; s123/s456/s789 are individual seed runs). All conditions have McNemar power $< 80\%$ for $|\Delta| = 2$\,pp (Appendix~\ref{app:power}). Degenerate conditions ($C_0 < 5\%$: QwQ-32B AIME$^\ddagger$ $n{=}22$, Qwen2.5-14B GSM8K$^\ddagger$ $n{=}30$) yield $\Delta = 0$ and are reported separately in Appendix~\ref{app:oracle}. $^\ddagger$Pilot conditions ($n{\leq}30$); included for coverage, not confirmatory evidence. Single-seed conditions use seed 123 (not selected post hoc).}
\label{tab:main_results}
